        "brief": "You're at the training kiosk with Brightwell's inbox open. Brightwell has an AI assistant that reads and summarises mail, so some emails may carry text hidden from the reader, such as white or tiny text, that the assistant would still read; use Show hidden text to look. Six things have come in: two supplier emails, two voicemails and two video calls. For each one, choose Trust, Report, Delete or Verify (ring the person back on a number you already hold, or check on a channel you trust), then tick what you noticed. Nobody will ask whether a voice or a face looked real: what counts is what each message asks you to do. Reporting or checking when you're unsure is always fine and never marked down, though a real one does take a colleague's time to confirm.",
